            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ai/plan-task",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "ai", "plan-task"]
            },
            "description": "### AI Provider Error Testing Scenarios:\n\n1. **Missing GROQ_API_KEY (HTTP 503)**:\n   - When `GROQ_API_KEY` is not set or empty in `.env`, the API safely returns HTTP 503 Service Unavailable without exposing credentials.\n\n2. **Invalid Model ID (HTTP 502)**:\n   - When `GROQ_MODEL` is unavailable or invalid, the API safely converts the provider error to HTTP 502 Bad Gateway.\n\n3. **Timeout (HTTP 504)**:\n   - If the request takes longer than `AI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` (e.g. 20000ms), the Groq SDK cancels the request and the API returns HTTP 504 Gateway Timeout.\n\n4. **Rate Limiting (HTTP 429)**:\n   - Exceeding `AI_RATE_LIMIT_MAX` (default 10 requests / 15 mins) triggers HTTP 429 Too Many Requests: `{\"success\":false,\"message\":\"Too many AI planning requests from this IP. Please try again later.\"}`.\n\n5. **Automated Mocks**:\n   - Provider scenarios (success, timeout, provider errors, malformed JSON, and rate limiting) are verified in `tests/ai.test.js` without exposing a real token."
          },
